# DAY4-SUMMARY.md — HealthNexus Command Center

**Day 54 of 60 · Core Feature Implementation**

## Milestone: The Incident Queue (System-Wide, Multi-Facility)

**What was built and why:** the product's front door — the screen a COO opens first. Every open synthetic incident across every facility, ranked by AI-derived severity (five-tier language), with a one-click facility filter and an at-a-glance summary strip. This is the first real feature UI of the capstone; everything before today was planning, environment, and data engine.

### Files Created

- `src/components/SummaryStrip.jsx` — total open incident count + per-tier breakdown
- `src/components/FacilityFilterBar.jsx` — "All Facilities" + per-facility filter chips
- `src/components/IncidentCard.jsx` — one incident row: severity badge (color + text), facility/unit/type, narrative, trend, relative time
- `src/components/IncidentQueue.jsx` — composes the above against `incidentState.js`; no new data logic, presentation only

### Files Modified

- `src/App.jsx` — replaced the Day 53 "Foundation Status" debug panel with the real Queue view; Resolved tab remains a stub until Day 57
- `src/theme.css` — added styles for the summary strip, facility chips, and incident cards
- `src/i18n/strings.js` — generalized the `comingSoon` string (was hardcoded to "Day 54")
- `scripts/build.js` — added the four new files to the bundle's dependency order

## Verified, Not Assumed

- **24 incidents rendered**, summary strip total matches exactly.
- **Facility filter tested live**: 24 → 7 incidents after selecting one facility, chip state updates correctly.
- **Click-through wired**: clicking a card surfaces the "full detail view is Day 55" stub note — confirms the interaction path exists even though the destination screen doesn't yet.
- **Zero console errors, zero horizontal overflow** at 1440px, 390px, and in Arabic/RTL.
- Caught and fixed one real bug before shipping: concatenating multiple component files each declaring `const { useState } = React;` at module scope collided once bundled (no ES modules at runtime, single shared scope). Fixed by using `React.useState`/`React.useMemo` directly instead of destructuring per-file.

## What's Ready for Day 55

`IncidentCard` already has an `onClick` wired to a `selectedIncidentId` state — Day 55's `IncidentDetail.jsx` just needs to render against that id instead of the current stub message.

## Key Learnings

01. A no-bundler concatenation approach means every file shares one scope — the same destructuring pattern that's fine in separate ES modules will collide the moment everything lands in one script tag.
02. The Summary Strip mattered more than expected: reading "24 open, 3 High Risk" before any incident narrative is what actually makes the screen feel like a COO tool instead of a raw list.
03. Wiring the click-through to a stub message, instead of leaving cards inert, made today's milestone honestly verifiable — a dead click and a labeled "not built yet" click look identical to a user but mean very different things during QA.
